From e514c6e92e1597da572796845ea5e0d51730174d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:58:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115-fxtec-pro1x: The jack detect
 switches are normally open
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The board described both headphone jack detect switches as normally
closed (qcom,hphl-jack-type-normally-closed and
qcom,ground-jack-type-normally-closed). The stock BENGAL IDP overlay of
this phone sets qcom,msm-mbhc-hphl-swh = <1> and gnd-swh = <1>, which
is what the mainline MBHC uses when the two properties are absent
(hphl_swh = gnd_swh = true). With them the plug logic was inverted:
an empty jack counted as inserted, MBHC measured the open microphone
line at boot (1787 mV against 1700 mV, "high impedance headphones",
reported as line out) and every real plug was reported as a removal.

Drop both properties. An earlier test that seemed to need them ran
before the SoundWire wake worked, when interrupts got through only
while a stream kept the bus awake.

Tested on the device: the Pro1-X headset is reported as a headset
(mic line about 1020 mV), both ALSA jack controls follow plug and
unplug, and PulseAudio switches to the headphone profile by itself.

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (the model compared the stock overlay with the driver's switch handling and wrote the change; the author plugged the headset for every test)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A2; flags=T; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=claude-opus-5-5; retrieval=none
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
index ddace69db..1d1ba8e1b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -415,12 +415,11 @@ wcd9370: audio-codec {
 		qcom,micbias4-microvolt = <1800000>;
 
 		/*
-		 * Both jack detect switches are normally closed (stock BENGAL IDP overlay:
-		 * qcom,msm-mbhc-hphl-swh = <1>, qcom,msm-mbhc-gnd-swh = <1>). Without this
-		 * MBHC never saw a plug: no insert or remove interrupt, the jack stayed off.
+		 * The jack detect switches are normally open: the stock BENGAL IDP
+		 * overlay sets qcom,msm-mbhc-hphl-swh = <1> and gnd-swh = <1>, which is
+		 * the mainline default (hphl_swh = gnd_swh = true without the
+		 * *-normally-closed properties).
 		 */
-		qcom,hphl-jack-type-normally-closed;
-		qcom,ground-jack-type-normally-closed;
 		qcom,mbhc-buttons-vthreshold-microvolt = <75000 150000 237000 500000 500000 500000 500000 500000>;
 		qcom,mbhc-headset-vthreshold-microvolt = <1700000>;
 		qcom,mbhc-headphone-vthreshold-microvolt = <50000>;
